{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011zu7fZCAXYDEotrY3aR4zv","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Dupree Ops LLC — Business Website\n     2→\n     3→Official business website for Dupree Ops, LLC. Built with Next.js, Tailwind CSS, and Supabase.\n     4→\n     5→## Features\n     6→\n     7→- **Services Page**: Showcase three core offerings with pricing and descriptions\n     8→- **Contact Form**: Accept inquiries with full validation and Supabase integration\n     9→- **Health Check**: `/api/health` endpoint for monitoring\n    10→- **Dark/Light Mode**: Theme toggle with persistent storage\n    11→- **Responsive Design**: Mobile, tablet, and desktop optimized\n    12→- **Analytics Tracking**: Page views and user interactions\n    13→- **WCAG Compliance**: Accessible forms and navigation\n    14→\n    15→## Tech Stack\n    16→\n    17→- **Framework**: Next.js 14\n    18→- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 3.3\n    19→- **Database**: Supabase (PostgreSQL)\n    20→- **Language**: TypeScript\n    21→- **Hosting**: Vercel\n    22→\n    23→## Setup\n    24→\n    25→### Prerequisites\n    26→\n    27→- Node.js 18+\n    28→- npm or yarn\n    29→- Supabase account (or use existing project)\n    30→\n    31→### Installation\n    32→\n    33→1. Clone the repository:\n    34→```bash\n    35→git clone https://github.com/IsaiahDupree/dupreeops-website.git\n    36→cd dupreeops-website\n    37→```\n    38→\n    39→2. Install dependencies:\n    40→```bash\n    41→npm install\n    42→```\n    43→\n    44→3. Configure environment variables:\n    45→```bash\n    46→# Copy the example file\n    47→cp .env.example .env.local\n    48→\n    49→# Edit .env.local with your Supabase credentials:\n    50→# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your_url_here\n    51→# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_key_here\n    52→# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_service_key_here\n    53→```\n    54→\n    55→4. Set up the database:\n    56→   - The migrations are automatically handled via Supabase\n    57→   - The `contact_submissions` table is created on deployment\n    58→   - RLS policies are configured for security\n    59→\n    60→5. Run the development server:\n    61→```bash\n    62→npm run dev\n    63→```\n    64→\n    65→Open [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000) in your browser.\n    66→\n    67→## Environment Variables\n    68→\n    69→| Variable | Description | Required |\n    70→|----------|-------------|----------|\n    71→| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` | Supabase project URL | Yes |\n    72→| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` | Supabase anonymous key | Yes |\n    73→| `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` | Supabase service role key (API only) | Yes |\n    74→\n    75→**Note**: Variables prefixed with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` are exposed to the browser. Never store sensitive secrets in these variables.\n    76→\n    77→## Project Structure\n    78→\n    79→```\n    80→.\n    81→├── pages/\n    82→│   ├── api/\n    83→│   │   ├── contact.ts       # Contact form API endpoint\n    84→│   │   └── health.ts        # Health check endpoint\n    85→│   ├── _app.tsx             # Next.js app wrapper\n    86→│   ├── index.tsx            # Homepage\n    87→│   ├── services.tsx         # Services listing page\n    88→│   ├── contact.tsx          # Contact page\n    89→│   └── [other pages]\n    90→├── components/\n    91→│   └── ContactForm.tsx      # Contact form with validation\n    92→├── lib/\n    93→│   ├── supabase.ts          # Supabase client config\n    94→│   ├── validation.ts        # Form validation logic\n    95→│   └── analytics.ts         # Analytics tracking\n    96→├── data/\n    97→│   └── services.ts          # Service offerings data\n    98→├── styles/\n    99→│   └── globals.css          # Global styles\n   100→├── public/                  # Static assets\n   101→└── vercel.json             # Vercel deployment config\n   102→```\n   103→\n   104→## Available Pages\n   105→\n   106→- `/` — Homepage with company information\n   107→- `/services` — Service offerings and pricing\n   108→- `/contact` — Contact form and contact information\n   109→- `/billing` — Billing and messaging policies\n   110→- `/terms` — Terms of service\n   111→- `/privacy` — Privacy policy\n   112→- `/sms` — SMS messaging policy\n   113→\n   114→## API Endpoints\n   115→\n   116→### Health Check\n   117→```\n   118→GET /api/health\n   119→```\n   120→\n   121→Returns service health status:\n   122→```json\n   123→{\n   124→  \"status\": \"healthy\",\n   125→  \"timestamp\": \"2024-04-18T21:00:00.000Z\",\n   126→  \"service\": \"dupreeops-website\",\n   127→  \"version\": \"1.0.0\"\n   128→}\n   129→```\n   130→\n   131→### Contact Form Submission\n   132→```\n   133→POST /api/contact\n   134→```\n   135→\n   136→Request:\n   137→```json\n   138→{\n   139→  \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n   140→  \"email\": \"john@example.com\",\n   141→  \"message\": \"I'd like to discuss your services...\"\n   142→}\n   143→```\n   144→\n   145→Response (success):\n   146→```json\n   147→{\n   148→  \"success\": true,\n   149→  \"message\": \"Contact form submitted successfully\",\n   150→  \"id\": \"uuid\"\n   151→}\n   152→```\n   153→\n   154→Response (error):\n   155→```json\n   156→{\n   157→  \"success\": false,\n   158→  \"message\": \"Validation failed\",\n   159→  \"errors\": [\n   160→    {\n   161→      \"field\": \"email\",\n   162→      \"message\": \"Invalid email format\"\n   163→    }\n   164→  ]\n   165→}\n   166→```\n   167→\n   168→## Building & Deployment\n   169→\n   170→### Local Build\n   171→```bash\n   172→npm run build\n   173→npm run start\n   174→```\n   175→\n   176→### Vercel Deployment\n   177→\n   178→The project is configured for automatic deployment via Vercel:\n   179→\n   180→1. Push to the main branch\n   181→2. Vercel automatically builds and deploys\n   182→3. Environment variables are configured in Vercel dashboard\n   183→\n   184→Manual deployment:\n   185→```bash\n   186→npm install -g vercel\n   187→vercel --prod\n   188→```\n   189→\n   190→## Form Validation\n   191→\n   192→The contact form includes both client-side and server-side validation:\n   193→\n   194→**Client-side**:\n   195→- Name: 2-100 characters\n   196→- Email: Valid email format\n   197→- Message: 10-5000 characters\n   198→\n   199→**Server-side**: Same rules applied on API endpoint\n   200→\n   201→Validation errors are returned with specific field messages for user guidance.\n   202→\n   203→## Database Schema\n   204→\n   205→### contact_submissions table\n   206→\n   207→```sql\n   208→CREATE TABLE contact_submissions (\n   209→  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n   210→  name TEXT NOT NULL,\n   211→  email TEXT NOT NULL,\n   212→  message TEXT NOT NULL,\n   213→  created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW(),\n   214→  updated_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()\n   215→);\n   216→```\n   217→\n   218→**Row Level Security (RLS)**:\n   219→- Anonymous users can insert (for contact form)\n   220→- Authenticated users can view and delete\n   221→- Admin-only delete access recommended\n   222→\n   223→## Performance\n   224→\n   225→- Static site generation for pages (near-instant load times)\n   226→- Optimized images and assets\n   227→- Database indexes for fast queries\n   228→- CDN distribution via Vercel\n   229→\n   230→## Monitoring\n   231→\n   232→Health check endpoint (`/api/health`) can be monitored for uptime:\n   233→```bash\n   234→curl https://dupreeops.com/api/health\n   235→```\n   236→\n   237→## Support & Issues\n   238→\n   239→For support inquiries:\n   240→- **Email**: support@dupreeops.com\n   241→- **Business**: hello@dupreeops.com\n   242→\n   243→## License\n   244→\n   245→© 2026 Dupree Ops, LLC. All rights reserved.\n   246→\n   247→## Contributing\n   248→\n   249→This is a private project. External contributions are not accepted at this time.\n   250→\n   251→---\n   252→\n   253→**Built with care by Dupree Ops, LLC**\n   254→\n   255→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0b6fff0-4192-4f9e-9ee3-3ef453685716","uuid":"29242058-6d99-4372-be30-f29207606b6b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/isaiahdupree/Documents/Software/DupreeOpsLLC/README.md","content":"# Dupree Ops LLC — Business Website\n\nOfficial business website for Dupree Ops, LLC. Built with Next.js, Tailwind CSS, and Supabase.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Services Page**: Showcase three core offerings with pricing and descriptions\n- **Contact Form**: Accept inquiries with full validation and Supabase integration\n- **Health Check**: `/api/health` endpoint for monitoring\n- **Dark/Light Mode**: Theme toggle with persistent storage\n- **Responsive Design**: Mobile, tablet, and desktop optimized\n- **Analytics Tracking**: Page views and user interactions\n- **WCAG Compliance**: Accessible forms and navigation\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- **Framework**: Next.js 14\n- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 3.3\n- **Database**: Supabase (PostgreSQL)\n- **Language**: TypeScript\n- **Hosting**: Vercel\n\n## Setup\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- Node.js 18+\n- npm or yarn\n- Supabase account (or use existing project)\n\n### Installation\n\n1. Clone the repository:\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/IsaiahDupree/dupreeops-website.git\ncd dupreeops-website\n```\n\n2. Install dependencies:\n```bash\nnpm install\n```\n\n3. Configure environment variables:\n```bash\n# Copy the example file\ncp .env.example .env.local\n\n# Edit .env.local with your Supabase credentials:\n# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your_url_here\n# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_key_here\n# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_service_key_here\n```\n\n4. Set up the database:\n   - The migrations are automatically handled via Supabase\n   - The `contact_submissions` table is created on deployment\n   - RLS policies are configured for security\n\n5. Run the development server:\n```bash\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nOpen [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000) in your browser.\n\n## Environment Variables\n\n| Variable | Description | Required |\n|----------|-------------|----------|\n| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` | Supabase project URL | Yes |\n| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` | Supabase anonymous key | Yes |\n| `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` | Supabase service role key (API only) | Yes |\n\n**Note**: Variables prefixed with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` are exposed to the browser. Never store sensitive secrets in these variables.\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n.\n├── pages/\n│   ├── api/\n│   │   ├── contact.ts       # Contact form API endpoint\n│   │   └── health.ts        # Health check endpoint\n│   ├── _app.tsx             # Next.js app wrapper\n│   ├── index.tsx            # Homepage\n│   ├── services.tsx         # Services listing page\n│   ├── contact.tsx          # Contact page\n│   └── [other pages]\n├── components/\n│   └── ContactForm.tsx      # Contact form with validation\n├── lib/\n│   ├── supabase.ts          # Supabase client config\n│   ├── validation.ts        # Form validation logic\n│   └── analytics.ts         # Analytics tracking\n├── data/\n│   └── services.ts          # Service offerings data\n├── styles/\n│   └── globals.css          # Global styles\n├── public/                  # Static assets\n└── vercel.json             # Vercel deployment config\n```\n\n## Available Pages\n\n- `/` — Homepage with company information\n- `/services` — Service offerings and pricing\n- `/contact` — Contact form and contact information\n- `/billing` — Billing and messaging policies\n- `/terms` — Terms of service\n- `/privacy` — Privacy policy\n- `/sms` — SMS messaging policy\n\n## API Endpoints\n\n### Health Check\n```\nGET /api/health\n```\n\nReturns service health status:\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"healthy\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2024-04-18T21:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"service\": \"dupreeops-website\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\"\n}\n```\n\n### Contact Form Submission\n```\nPOST /api/contact\n```\n\nRequest:\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n  \"email\": \"john@example.com\",\n  \"message\": \"I'd like to discuss your services...\"\n}\n```\n\nResponse (success):\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"message\": \"Contact form submitted successfully\",\n  \"id\": \"uuid\"\n}\n```\n\nResponse (error):\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": false,\n  \"message\": \"Validation failed\",\n  \"errors\": [\n    {\n      \"field\": \"email\",\n      \"message\": \"Invalid email format\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Building & Deployment\n\n### Local Build\n```bash\nnpm run build\nnpm run start\n```\n\n### Vercel Deployment\n\nThe project is configured for automatic deployment via Vercel:\n\n1. Push to the main branch\n2. Vercel automatically builds and deploys\n3. Environment variables are configured in Vercel dashboard\n\nManual deployment:\n```bash\nnpm install -g vercel\nvercel --prod\n```\n\n## Form Validation\n\nThe contact form includes both client-side and server-side validation:\n\n**Client-side**:\n- Name: 2-100 characters\n- Email: Valid email format\n- Message: 10-5000 characters\n\n**Server-side**: Same rules applied on API endpoint\n\nValidation errors are returned with specific field messages for user guidance.\n\n## Database Schema\n\n### contact_submissions table\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE contact_submissions (\n  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  name TEXT NOT NULL,\n  email TEXT NOT NULL,\n  message TEXT NOT NULL,\n  created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW(),\n  updated_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()\n);\n```\n\n**Row Level Security (RLS)**:\n- Anonymous users can insert (for contact form)\n- Authenticated users can view and delete\n- Admin-only delete access recommended\n\n## Performance\n\n- Static site generation for pages (near-instant load times)\n- Optimized images and assets\n- Database indexes for fast queries\n- CDN distribution via Vercel\n\n## Monitoring\n\nHealth check endpoint (`/api/health`) can be monitored for uptime:\n```bash\ncurl https://dupreeops.com/api/health\n```\n\n## Support & Issues\n\nFor support inquiries:\n- **Email**: support@dupreeops.com\n- **Business**: hello@dupreeops.com\n\n## License\n\n© 2026 Dupree Ops, LLC. All rights reserved.\n\n## Contributing\n\nThis is a private project. External contributions are not accepted at this time.\n\n---\n\n**Built with care by Dupree Ops, LLC**\n\n","numLines":255,"startLine":1,"totalLines":255}}}
